<!-- ========== 1. EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW ========== -->
<section id="executive-overview">
    <h2>1. Executive Overview</h2>
    <p>This report analyzes <strong>{kpis['total_observations']} monthly observations</strong> of global crude oil prices spanning from <strong>{kpis['first_date'].strftime('%B %Y')}</strong> to <strong>{kpis['last_date'].strftime('%B %Y')}</strong> — a period of over {kpis['years']:.0f} years. All figures are derived exclusively from the source dataset; no external data has been fabricated or assumed.</p>

    <p>Crude oil prices have undergone a profound structural transformation over this period. Beginning at just <strong>${kpis['first_price']:.2f}/bbl</strong> in January 1970, prices reached an all-time high of <strong>${kpis['max_price']:.2f}/bbl</strong> in {kpis['max_date'].strftime('%B %Y')}, representing an overall range of <strong>${kpis['overall_range']:.2f}</strong>. The compound annual growth rate stands at <strong>{kpis['cagr']:.2f}%</strong>, though this steady long-run metric masks extraordinary short-term volatility — the dataset's standard deviation of <strong>${kpis['std_dev']:.2f}</strong> underscores the extent of price dispersion.</p>

    <p>Key findings include:</p>
    <ul style="margin-left:20px; margin-bottom:12px;">
        <li>The <strong>{kpis['highest_decade']}</strong> recorded the highest average price at <strong>${kpis['highest_decade_val']:.2f}/bbl</strong>.</li>
        <li>The largest single-month price move was <strong>{"+" if kpis['mom_abs_val']>0 else ""}${kpis['mom_abs_val']:.2f}</strong> in {kpis['mom_abs_date'].strftime('%B %Y')}.</li>
        <li>The biggest annual gain was <strong>{biggest_annual_gain_val:+.1f}%</strong> in {biggest_annual_gain_yr}, while the largest annual decline was <strong>{biggest_annual_loss_val:+.1f}%</strong> in {biggest_annual_loss_yr}.</li>
        <li>The median monthly price is <strong>${kpis['median_price']:.2f}</strong>, well below the mean of <strong>${kpis['mean_price']:.2f}</strong>, indicating a right-skewed distribution driven by periodic price spikes.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<!-- ========== 2. LONG-TERM TRAJECTORY ========== -->
<section id="long-term-trend">
    <h2>2. Long-Term Price Trajectory (1970–2026)</h2>
    <p>The chart below presents the complete monthly time series of crude oil prices, annotated with the major geopolitical and economic events that shaped the global oil market over five decades.</p>

    <div class="chart-container">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['long_term']}" alt="Long-term crude oil price trajectory 1970-2026">
    </div>

    <p>The trajectory reveals several distinct price regimes:</p>
    <ul style="margin-left:20px; margin-bottom:12px;">
        <li><strong>1970–1973 (Pre-embargo stability):</strong> Prices remained flat near $1–$2/bbl, reflecting the era of regulated oil markets.</li>
        <li><strong>1973–1981 (Twin oil shocks):</strong> Two convulsive spikes — the 1973 embargo and the 1979 Iranian Revolution — pushed prices from $2.70 to $40.75, a 15x increase in under 7 years.</li>
        <li><strong>1982–1999 (Long consolidation):</strong> A two-decade range-bound period, generally between $10 and $35, punctuated by the 1986 collapse and the 1990 Gulf War spike.</li>
        <li><strong>2000–2008 (Commodity supercycle):</strong> A sustained bull run that peaked at ${kpis['max_price']:.2f} in {kpis['max_date'].strftime('%B %Y')}, followed by a dramatic crash.</li>
        <li><strong>2009–2014 (Post-crisis recovery):</strong> Prices rebounded to $100+ levels, sustained by emerging market demand.</li>
        <li><strong>2014–2020 (Shale era &amp; pandemic):</strong> Structural oversupply and the COVID-19 shock pushed prices as low as ${df[df['Year']==2020]['Crude_Oil_Price'].min():.2f}/bbl.</li>
        <li><strong>2021–2026 (Recovery &amp; moderation):</strong> Prices surged on post-pandemic demand and geopolitical disruption, then moderated to the $60–$88 range.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="chart-container">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['annual_avg']}" alt="Annual average crude oil prices">
    </div>

    <div class="chart-container">
        <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['yoy']}" alt="Year-over-year price changes">
    </div>
</section>

