    <div class="callout">
        <strong>Observation:</strong> The largest absolute moves cluster in periods of high price levels (2008, 2022), while the largest percentage moves are more prominent in low-price transition periods (1973–1974, 1986, 1999). This distinction matters for risk modeling — percentage volatility can be extreme even when absolute dollar moves appear modest.
    </div>

    <h3>Rolling Volatility</h3>
